course: dictionary
lesson: 7394
title: Serious words about health
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words in health texts are new, but the sentences around them often explain them. Look for clues before you reach for a dictionary. «When Nan gets pneumonia, a bad chest illness, Mrs Dobbs leaves soup on the step.» The words after the comma, «a bad chest illness», tell you what pneumonia is.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. Pneumonia is a serious illness, so you could say «When Nan gets a serious illness of the lungs, Mrs Dobbs leaves soup». That still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Some clues tell you where or how. «Antibiotics have saved millions of lives from infections... such as infected wounds and pneumonia, an infection of the lungs.» The phrase «an infection of the lungs» tells you where pneumonia happens. An infection is an illness caused by germs.
fact: Pneumonia is a serious illness in which the lungs become swollen and fill with fluid.
fact: Pneumonia is often caused by germs, and it makes it hard to breathe.
fact: Doctors treat pneumonia, and it can be dangerous for babies and old people.
fact: Vaccines help prevent some kinds of pneumonia.
fact: Pneumonia is an uncountable noun, so we say «have pneumonia», not «have a pneumonias».
exercise: «When Nan gets pneumonia, a bad chest illness, Mrs Dobbs leaves soup on the step.» What is pneumonia? | A type of cold weather | *A serious illness of the lungs | A kind of soup | A step on the stairs
exercise: «Antibiotics have saved millions of lives from infections... such as pneumonia, an infection of the lungs.» Which part of the body does pneumonia affect? | The heart | The legs | The skin | *The lungs
exercise: «Measles can cause pneumonia and brain swelling.» What can measles cause, according to the sentence? | Sunburn and hair loss | Colds only | *Pneumonia and brain swelling | Broken bones
test: Pneumonia makes it hard to do what? | Walk | Hear | Sleep | *Breathe
test: Which can help prevent some kinds of pneumonia? | Sweets | Loud music | *Vaccines | Ice cream
exam: What does pneumonia mean? | A bone that breaks | A kind of food | *A serious illness where the lungs swell and fill with fluid | A small cough that goes away in a day
